<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Different Quantization Precisions.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From Tab. <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Different Quantization Precisions. ‣ 4.3 Ablation Studies ‣ 4 Experiment ‣ PAHQ: Accelerating Automated Circuit Discovery through Mixed-Precision Inference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, it is evident that different quantization precisions significantly impact model performance. 4-bit quantization severely compromises model accuracy and faithfulness. We believe that this is because the precise activation value output by the selected edge is passed, the number of bits of the weights and output activation values of subsequent layers is too small, so small numerical changes cannot be retained. Therefore, it is almost impossible to use 4-bit quantization. In contrast, 16-bit quantization offers minimal precision improvements compared to 8-bit. To prove the correctness of our quantization method, we tested the performance of the model under different quantization scales. See Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Quantization Strategy ‣ PAHQ: Accelerating Automated Circuit Discovery through Mixed-Precision Inference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> for details.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S4.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S4.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T5.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S4.T5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="S4.T5.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Precision</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S4.T5.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="S4.T5.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Accuracy</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S4.T5.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:56.9pt;">
<span id="S4.T5.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">AUC-ROC</span>
</span></td></tr>
