<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Performance comparison between Edge Pruning and PAHQ across different dataset sizes and training steps.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A key practical consideration is computational resource usage. PAHQ completes circuit discovery in 22 minutes using only 5 GB of GPU memory, whereas Edge Pruning requires 33 GB of GPU memory and approximately 3.5 hours for comparable performance. This substantial reduction in memory footprint enables PAHQ to run on modest-memory GPUs, making it significantly more accessible in resource-limited environments.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">While Edge Pruning can achieve lower KL divergence with sufficient training steps and computational resources, PAHQ offers a compelling trade-off between performance and practical constraints. The modest increase in KL divergence (0.83 vs. 0.19-0.27 for Edge Pruning at 3000 steps) is offset by dramatic improvements in memory efficiency and runtime, making circuit discovery accessible to researchers with limited computational resources.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Quantization Strategy</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix provides a detailed ablation study comparing PAHQ’s selective quantization strategy against full-network quantization approaches to demonstrate the effectiveness of our targeted precision preservation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Experimental Design</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To validate PAHQ’s quantization strategy, we conducted a systematic comparison between selective quantization (our approach) and global quantization methods. The experiment follows a two-phase incremental quantization protocol:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase 1: Non-critical Component Quantization</span>
We begin with the full-precision circuit discovered by ACDC. Following the model’s reverse topological order, we iteratively select additional attention heads classified as non-critical and quantize their weights from FP32 to FP8, while preserving all critical components in FP32 precision. We record the overall task accuracy after each incremental quantization step.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase 2: Critical Component Quantization</span>
After all non-critical attention heads have been quantized to FP8, we systematically quantize the remaining critical attention head weights from FP32 to FP8 in 10% increments until all weights are quantized. At each step, we measure the impact on task performance to understand the sensitivity of critical components to precision reduction.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.23264v1/figure/quantization.png" id="A5.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/235;" width="476" height="235" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>The results of quantization strategy comparison.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Results and Analysis</h3>

<figure id="A5.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.23264v1/method.svg" id="A5.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/240;" width="381" height="240"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>The full algorithm and implementation of PAHQ.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ E.1 Experimental Design ‣ Appendix E Quantization Strategy ‣ PAHQ: Accelerating Automated Circuit Discovery through Mixed-Precision Inference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> presents the results of our quantization strategy comparison. The experimental results confirm two key findings:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A uniform 8-bit quantization approach, which quantizes both critical and non-critical components simultaneously, results in substantial accuracy degradation. This demonstrates that treating all network components equally during quantization is suboptimal for maintaining task performance.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">PAHQ’s targeted preservation of FP32 precision on critical components while quantizing non-critical components to FP8 is essential for maintaining high accuracy under memory-constrained scenarios. This selective approach allows us to achieve significant memory savings without compromising the faithfulness of circuit discovery.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">These results provide empirical validation for PAHQ’s core design principle: the importance of maintaining high precision for components identified as critical by circuit discovery methods while safely reducing precision elsewhere. This targeted approach enables substantial computational savings without sacrificing the reliability of mechanistic interpretability analysis.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The findings also highlight the limitations of naive quantization approaches in the context of interpretability methods, where the preservation of critical pathway faithfulness is paramount. Our selective quantization strategy offers a principled solution to this challenge, making large-scale circuit discovery more computationally feasible.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Implement: Integration with ACDC</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide a detailed demonstration of how PAHQ readily integrates with the ACDC method. As mentioned in  <a href="#A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="Circuit Discovery. ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries ‣ PAHQ: Accelerating Automated Circuit Discovery through Mixed-Precision Inference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, ACDC is a powerful circuit discovery technique that identifies critical connections within the model by analyzing the impact of activation replacements on downstream computations. The algorithm below describes the implementation details of the PAHQ-ACDC integration, as shown in the Figure <a href="#A5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ E.2 Results and Analysis ‣ Appendix E Quantization Strategy ‣ PAHQ: Accelerating Automated Circuit Discovery through Mixed-Precision Inference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The specific algorithm is as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<div id="A6.p3.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_listing">
<div id="algx1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          Model with <math id="algx1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers and <math id="algx1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> heads per layer, clean input <math id="algx1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, corrupted input <math id="algx1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, initial computational graph <math id="algx1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math>, pruning threshold <math id="algx1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, activation replacement threshold <math id="algx1.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, maximum iteration steps <math id="algx1.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, change rate threshold <math id="algx1.l1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, weights <math id="algx1.l1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{comp,prec}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{comp,prec}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="algx1.l1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="comp\in\{Q,K,V,O\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">comp\in\{Q,K,V,O\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="algx1.l1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="prec\in\{8,32\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">prec\in\{8,32\}</annotation></semantics></math>. All 8-bit weights are pre-loaded on GPU.

</div>
<div id="algx1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          Sparse computational graph <math id="algx1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{sparse}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{sparse}</annotation></semantics></math> and final output

</div>
<div id="algx1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          Initialize scheduler <math id="algx1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\{\cdot\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\{\cdot\}</annotation></semantics></math> to control high-precision computation <math id="algx1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{high}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{high}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, low-precision computation <math id="algx1.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{low}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{low}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> and high-precision weight uploading <math id="algx1.l3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
          Initialize computational graph <math id="algx1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="algx1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> represents all attention heads and <math id="algx1.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> represents all possible edges

</div>
<div id="algx1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
          Initialize importance scores <math id="algx1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(e)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(e)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="algx1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in E</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
          Initialize current iteration step <math id="algx1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
          Initialize previous computational graph <math id="algx1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{prev}=G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{prev}=G</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
          <span id="algx1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="algx1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="algx1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|E|&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|E|&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="algx1.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{|E_{prev}|-|E|}{|E_{prev}|}&gt;\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{|E_{prev}|-|E|}{|E_{prev}|}&gt;\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
            <math id="algx1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{prev}\leftarrow E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{prev}\leftarrow E</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each edge <math id="algx1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in E</annotation></semantics></math> from source <math id="algx1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(l_{s},h_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(l_{s},h_{s})</annotation></semantics></math> to destination <math id="algx1.l10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(l_{d},h_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(l_{d},h_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
             // First inference: Get activations using clean input

</div>
<div id="algx1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
             <math id="algx1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{clean}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{clean}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Perform complete model inference with clean input <math id="algx1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, record source activation <math id="algx1.l12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{clean}^{(l_{s},h_{s})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{clean}^{(l_{s},h_{s})}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
             // Second inference: Get activations using corrupted input

</div>
<div id="algx1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
             <math id="algx1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{corrupt}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{corrupt}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Perform complete model inference with corrupted input <math id="algx1.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, record source activation <math id="algx1.l14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{corrupt}^{(l_{s},h_{s})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{corrupt}^{(l_{s},h_{s})}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
             // Third inference: Perform inference with activation replacement

</div>
<div id="algx1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
             Initialize dictionary for replaced activations <math id="algx1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{replaced}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{replaced}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
             <span id="algx1.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each layer <math id="algx1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in\{1,...,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in\{1,...,L\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
               <math id="algx1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{*}\leftarrow\begin{cases}h_{s},&amp;\text{if }l=l_{s}\\
-1,&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{*}\leftarrow\begin{cases}h_{s},&amp;\text{if }l=l_{s}\\
-1,&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
            
            
               <span id="algx1.l19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="algx1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{*}\neq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{*}\neq-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
